  "$comment": [
    "sha256 of every migration at or before declaration.json#sealedThrough, as audited in Phase 0.5.",
    "The seal is CLOSED: it never grows. A migration newer than sealedThrough is always classified in",
    "full, never hashed and waved through \u2014 so \"seal it and move on\" is not a path past the guard.",
    "It exempts these exact bytes from the per-statement hazard rules (history legitimately contains",
    "views without security_invoker and `grant all ... to anon`), and it is what makes the",
    "`raise exception` assertions inside the hand-written security migrations un-removable: editing one",
    "changes its hash. There is no regeneration command on purpose: re-sealing is a deliberate, reviewed",
    "act, and the entry count and sealedThrough are ALSO pinned as literals in migrationInvariants.test.ts,",
    "so it cannot be done without a second, loud diff in a .test.ts file."
  ],
